{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:spheres","title":"ex:spheres","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":239,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#ex:spheres","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:induced-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:euclidean-metric]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"ex:spheres","line":431,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Spheres]\n\\label{ex:spheres}\n\n\\uses{def:induced-metric, ex:euclidean-metric}\n\n\n\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.13}\nFor $n>0$, the unit sphere $S^n\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{n+1}$ carries the round (standard) metric induced by its inclusion $\\iota$. Its differential identifies $T_pS^n$ with $(\\mathbb Rp)^\\perp$, so $\\iota^*\\bar g$ is positive definite by Lemma \\ref{lem:pullback-immersion-metric}.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Spheres] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-65783a73706865726573\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ainduced-metric\">↗ def:induced-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23ex%3Aeuclidean-metric\">↗ ex:euclidean-metric</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.13</span></span>For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n&gt;0$\">$n&gt;0$</span>, the unit sphere <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S^n\\subseteq \\mathbb R^{n+1}$\">$S^n\\subseteq \\mathbb R^{n+1}$</span> carries the round (standard) metric induced by its inclusion <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\iota $\">$\\iota $</span>. Its differential identifies <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_pS^n$\">$T_pS^n$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(\\mathbb Rp)^\\perp $\">$(\\mathbb Rp)^\\perp $</span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\iota ^*\\bar g$\">$\\iota ^*\\bar g$</span> is positive definite by Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apullback-immersion-metric\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pullback-immersion-metric\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a70756c6c6261636b2d696d6d657273696f6e2d6d6574726963\">5</a>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:induced-metric","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:induced-metric","title":"def:induced-metric","label":"def:induced-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:euclidean-metric","title":"ex:euclidean-metric","label":"ex:euclidean-metric"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius","title":"lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius","label":"lem:sphere-tangent-orthogonal-radius"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:polar-map","title":"def:polar-map","label":"def:polar-map"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:spheres","title":"ex:spheres","tex":"\\begin{definition}[Spheres]\n\\label{ex:spheres}\n\n\\uses{